Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:11:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] Fix FidelityFX Vulkan context creation on unified
 memory GPUs

FidelityFX refuses host visible memory when it asks for device local
memory. On Adreno every usable device local type is host visible, so
FSR failed with a backend error before its first allocation.

While a FidelityFX Vulkan context is created, report one such type as
device local only, as long as another type can still serve uploads.
The memory properties hook is now always attached for this, and the
VRAM spoofing in it stays behind its config option.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A9WqnwGsLAcGJXd49N2pes
